{
    "_comment": [
        "QuickSite embed policy — INSTALL-WIDE, set at deployment.",
        "",
        "This is the shipped TEMPLATE. setup.sh / setup.bat copy it to",
        "embed-policy.json (beside this file) on first run when that file is",
        "absent; the live copy is gitignored and is the one the engine reads.",
        "Edit the live embed-policy.json, never this .example.",
        "",
        "It decides the sandbox an <iframe> in ANY project on this install is",
        "given, by the host of its src. It is the ONLY writer of that policy:",
        "there is no panel control and no command that changes it, so a signed-in",
        "user — owner or admin of a project included — cannot widen it. That is",
        "the whole reason it lives here rather than per project.",
        "",
        "FORMAT",
        "  default     array of sandbox tokens applied to an iframe whose src",
        "              host matches no entry in `hosts`. [] (empty) is the",
        "              strictest sandbox and blocks everything — the safe default.",
        "  hosts       array of { name, parameters } objects:",
        "                name        a bare host, e.g. \"youtube.com\". Matching is",
        "                            CSP-style: it also covers every subdomain",
        "                            (www.youtube.com, m.youtube.com), never a",
        "                            look-alike (fakeyoutube.com).",
        "                parameters  array of sandbox tokens granted to that host.",
        "",
        "  Valid tokens: allow-scripts, allow-same-origin, allow-forms,",
        "  allow-popups, allow-modals, allow-orientation-lock, allow-pointer-lock,",
        "  allow-presentation, allow-downloads.",
        "",
        "  Always stripped, whatever you write: allow-top-navigation,",
        "  allow-top-navigation-by-user-activation,",
        "  allow-top-navigation-to-custom-protocols, allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox.",
        "  Any token outside the valid list above is dropped too, and the drop is",
        "  written to the error log naming the token.",
        "  allow-scripts + allow-same-origin together is also refused for any",
        "  same-origin or relative src, and a host entry naming this install's own",
        "  host is ignored — both would hand a frame script access to this origin.",
        "",
        "  Only <iframe> is governed. sandbox does nothing on <video>/<audio>.",
        "",
        "Every entry below is inherited by every project and every built site, so",
        "add a host only when you mean to trust it. The shipped default trusts",
        "YouTube, the host QuickSite projects most commonly embed.",
        "",
        "These host names are READABLE by every authenticated member of this",
        "install: the panel shows the policy read-only, so a host you list here is",
        "disclosed to anyone who can sign in. Do not treat a host name as a secret.",
        "",
        "This whole _comment key is ignored by the engine; it is documentation."
    ],
    "default": [],
    "hosts": [
        { "name": "youtube.com", "parameters": ["allow-scripts", "allow-same-origin", "allow-presentation"] }
    ]
}
